privateData.editorialMd:
Build the result list

Keep the first copy of each number in readings. Skip any later copies of the same number. Keep the order in which the numbers first appear. For [4, 2, 4, 3, 2], the result list is [4, 2, 3].

Return the answer

Count the even numbers in the result list. An even number divides by 2 with no remainder. Count 0 and negative even numbers too. Return the count. An empty list gives 0.

Why this works

Each value in the result list follows Step 1. Step 2 uses only those values. Keeping these steps separate helps avoid returning the list when the question asks for one number. Check empty input, one item, repeated values, and the largest allowed input.

Efficiency goal: time O(n); extra memory, including the result list, O(n). n is the input length. These labels describe how work and memory grow with the input.

